  }
  // LEAKED: add(index,e), remove(index), set(), clear(), subList()...
  // caller: stack.add(0, forgedTxn);  → LIFO invariant destroyed
  // base change: if ArrayList.add() starts calling addAll(), overrides
  //              can recurse unexpectedly → self-use fragility.

  // FIX — COMPOSITION + DELEGATION
  class TxnUndoStack {
     private final Deque<Txn> store = new ArrayDeque<>();   // HAS-A
     void push(Txn t){ store.push(t); }
     Txn  pop(){ return store.pop(); }
     boolean isEmpty(){ return store.isEmpty(); }
     // EXPOSES ONLY stack ops — no list surface area leaks
  }

  SOLID: ISP (expose minimal interface) + LSP (don't inherit wrong contract).
  Rule: inherit only a TRUE is-a with a stable base; else compose.
  Note: java.util.Stack extends Vector — the JDK's own cautionary tale.
```
